4c (c) E3-O AS STATED, THE HOLD IN E5 ONLY: in E3-O the heat stage runs with every radio C1 leaves on (no hold); in E5 a step
   of the kit's controls beyond the heat stage holds the charge (as H1), idles the running module (no shutdown) and powers off
   board D (APRS), the PA rail, the RockBLOCK (RB_SW_EN), the LoRa module (LORA_ON), both E72 (ZB_ON) and the Geiger module
   (GEIGER_EN). H1's own actions, which it reuses (CONOPS 4c): "through board A's expanders on the kit bus it turns off the monitor, the pack heater, board D, PoE, the USB-C outlet, the wall port's VBUS and the PA and HF software holds; it holds the charge by the charger's own charge-inhibit bit". Heat in E5 under it: 19.497 W (MODELED,
   plan; 18.152 W at the pack); as board B is generated, the 5G socket's supply dropped too, 19.497 W. Each part routed by the
   air needs (MODELED, E3-O with the heat stage / E5 with the hold):
      RB9704    1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      LIME      1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      SA868     1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      PCM2912A  1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      G6K       1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      H5007NL   1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      ATP16     1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      PXP4043C  1.806 / 2.159 W/K
      SGP41     1.806 / 2.159 W/K  (its absolute rating's screen only: survival INCONCLUSIVE)
      XENARC    1.083 / 1.079 W/K
      CM5       0.903 / 0.863 W/K
      SOUNDER   0.903 / 0.863 W/K
      NVME      0.903 / 0.863 W/K
      AW7915    0.774 / 0.720 W/K
      RM520N    0.774 / 0.720 W/K
   so the line is G_c = 2.159 W/K, set by E5 (E3-O alone 1.806 W/K); 2.399 with 1 K and 2.698 with 2 K of margin; with the module
   at its typical 4.5 W in the hold 2.443 W/K; at HIGH heat 4.304 W/K (not covered). Over the low case's cap by 0.058 W/K, inside
   W4's range and under 32.53's: CONDITIONAL on T-H1. Not routed by the air:
      ATP19     its limit 55 C (operating, powered) is at or under E3-O's ambient
      EPAPER    its limit 60 C (operating, unpowered, inside a range it may operate in (INFERRED to cover it unpowered)) is at or under E5's ambient
4d THE HOLD'S TRIGGER WINDOW at the line (it must not act in E3-O, and must act in E5 before the radios it turns off pass
   their +70 C): E3-O's steady mixed air with the radios on 67.55 C; the mixed air by which E5 needs the hold 70.00 C; window 2.45 K.
   Taken from it: the reference's error twice (board B's TMP117, +-0.2 C to 100 C, MAKER p.1), E5's fastest rise 15.0 K/h (the
   chamber's 30 to 60 C in 2 h, Method 507.6 as L4-E10 transcribed it) times a 61 s reading and response lag (ASSUMPTION):
   0.254167 K. What is left bounds the reference's offset to the air at the +70 C parts: at most +-0.899099 K (INFERRED). The TMP117 is
   a board sensor under the coolers: across the exhaust's 0 to 5.64 K the window is -3.84 K, so it DOES NOT EXIST unless the
   reference is placed in the mixed air near those parts or its offset is calibrated at T-H1 to +-0.899099 K (CONDITIONAL); with the
   whole spread it would need 3.111 W/K. The trigger then sits at the window's middle, 68.65 C of mixed air plus the calibrated
   offset; restore 5 K under it after 30 minutes (PROVISIONAL). The window grows with the conductance: 2.45 K at 2.159 W/K; 4.17 K at 2.500 W/K; 5.00 K at 2.709 W/K.
   Inside the envelope the air is 52.55 C at the line, far under it. In E5 under the hold the mixed air settles at 70.00 C.
4e If T-H1 reads under the line: the radio modules (RockBLOCK, board D) and the LimeSDR coupled to the plate hold E3-O at the
   plate's 62.6..66.8 C at the floor (3.22 K inside +70 C at its upper fraction) and E5 under the hold at 66.0..69.4 C (0.61 K) (INFERRED);
   the SGP41 in the bay air (72.95 C in E5) is then past Table 5's +70 C short-term storage, an absolute rating (the owner's
   question of 6 covers it).
