   E U13 at its rail's declared typical   0.595 W (INFERRED): DBV E3-O 205.1 C, E5 207.5 C; DRV E3-O 127.2 C, E5 129.6 C
   C U5 at its rail's declared typical    0.253 W (INFERRED): DBV E3-O 126.1 C, E5 128.5 C; DRV E3-O 92.9 C, E5 95.4 C
   The DRV package holds U13 at the plan load and U5 at its declared typical; at U13's declared 0.35 A neither package holds
   (a DRV part takes at most 0.323 A at E5's air): a buck, or the rail's load re-derived. Owed to boards E and C's owners.
5d THE SGP41 (board E U17). CHO-001 picks it for the battery bay ("SGP41 in the battery bay (32.54)"); REQ-042: "Water on the
   case floor, and hydrogen or VOC in the battery bay, raise an alarm and shut the pack down."; CFL-002's acceptance: "The SGP41
   is fitted where the battery bay's air is sampled, or an owner ruling drops it; the envelope's hot end is not recomputed until
   one of the two happens.".
   Its maker's conditions (1j): its gas specifications hold only when it is stored at 5 to 30 C and operated at -10 to +50 C
   (section 2.3 and Table 4, p.6), and "Prolonged exposure to conditions outside these conditions may reduce sensor performance"
   (p.6); Table 5's -20 to +55 C operating and -40 to +70 C short-term storage are absolute (p.7).
   The reference: a TMP117 on the SGP41's carrier, +-0.15 C maximum from -40 to 70 C (MAKER, TMP117 p.1); the BME688's +-0.5 C
   sits in Table 10's Typ column (p.14), not a bound, and is not used. The gradient to the SGP41 at most 0.5 K with its own
   heating (ASSUMPTION, a placement rule measured at the bench); the lag 0.254167 K (E5's 15.0 K/h, the fastest rise the record
   carries, times a 61 s reading and response, ASSUMPTION).
   Power off at a reading of 55 - 0.15 - 0.5 - 0.254167 = 54.095833 C, set at 54.0 C (rounded down): the SGP41 is at most
   54.904167 C when switched off, 0.095833 K under Table 5's +55 C. Power on and use of its output at a reading at or under 50 -
   0.15 - 0.5 - 0.254167 = 49.095833 C, set at 49.0 C: at most 49.904167 C while its output is used. Between the two it stays
   powered, its output logged as outside Table 4 and not used for REQ-042; off at every start until the reading is at or under
   49.0 C.
   In the envelope (+40 C) its channel works only where the reference reads at or under 49.0 C in every state, with 0.5 K kept
   for a bounded restart: the location's own temperature at or under 48.35 C. The binding state is the heat stage, 27.086 W with
   the ballasts, lid open or closed (E3-L runs it at +40 C lid closed); C1 holds the other states' air at its +50 C on board B's
   TMP117 plus 0.2 C and the lag, 50.454 C. The locations that still sample the bay air (fraction of the air's rise from W4's
   films, INFERRED; local temperatures MODELED at +40 C):
      location                                           fraction     needs      lid open, line lid closed, 32.53 2.0/1.5 C1-held
      the bay air where board E's U17 sits (as designed) 1.000-1.000  3.244 W/K  52.55 C        53.54 / 58.06 C        50.45 C
      the east wall's inner skin in the pack pocket      0.541-0.781  2.535 W/K  49.80 C        50.58 / 54.11 C        48.17 C
      the floor's inner skin under the pack              0.588-0.898  2.912 W/K  51.27 C        52.16 / 56.21 C        49.39 C
   The coolest is the east wall's inner skin in the pack pocket (the pack keeps 7.38 mm to that wall at the worst, CASE-MARGINS
   M4b; a carrier bonded to the skin, the SGP41 sampling the bay air through a diffusion port whose response is owed to the
   bench). It needs 2.535 W/K with the lid open, inside W4's 2.85 and under 32.53's 3.0; and the same 2.535 W/K with the lid
   closed, over 32.53's 1.5 to 2.0 and over W4's high case 2.49: NOT HELD with the lid closed on any conductance the record
   carries. Where it holds: the C1-held states 48.17 C (0.18 K to spare); a warm start from the envelope's +45 C storage
   (powered at once); recovery from E3-O's end (63.35 C at the skin at 2.535 W/K) to a restart in 2.98 to 3.73 h at +40 C
   (32.53's 8 to 10 kJ/K).
   Storage in the envelope: -20 to +45 C for three months (-20 to +25 C for a year, pcb_envelope.yaml) against Table 4's 5 to 30
   C storage: an unpowered kit's inside sits at the ambient, so no location changes it.
   At the margins it is off (E3-O starts from a kit at +55 C, so it is never powered there; in E5 it is off from 54.0 C). At the
   line, in the bay air 67.55 C (E3-O) and 70.00 C (E5), at the skin 64.80 and 67.81 C, under Table 5's +70 C short-term
   storage, an absolute rating: INCONCLUSIVE, Sensirion's duration and recovery owed (drafted); in a cooler's exhaust it would
   pass it (72.78 C in E5), so it stays out of it. A supply switch and a bus of its own keep a live pin from feeding it (record,
   section 6).
   RESULT: no location holds the SGP41 inside its maker's conditions in the envelope: not with the lid closed at the hot end (no
   conductance the record carries reaches 2.535 W/K) and not in storage. CHO-001 binds the part: the owner's question (6b).
5e What stays CONDITIONAL: T-H1 lid open with fans at or over 2.159 W/K; the hold's reference calibrated to +-0.899099 K or
   placed in the mixed air; the SGP41's shutdown at the margins (a TMP117 on its carrier within 0.5 K, its switch and bus,
   Sensirion's duration) and, inside the envelope, the owner's answer (6b); the pushbuttons' pick; PDi's statement; the
   regulators; the +70 C parts out of the exhaust; the fans' rating, the other lines with no range held and the lines cleared
   only by an absolute rating (7d).

6 The owner-question test, after the engineering routes of 4 and 5 are assessed
6a At the margins, a part with every route rejected or outside authority on held evidence: none.
6b Inside the envelope: the SGP41 (5d), RAISED. The conflict is CFL-002's: CHO-001's SGP41 in the battery bay against REQ-042's
   VOC channel under D-02a's "operate to specification inside the envelope". The options:
   A  a BME688-class gas sensor in the bay in its place (Bosch: gas sensing -40 to +85 C, p.8, "The sensors are electrically
      operable within this range. Actual performance may vary."; its IAQ figures "Tested with 0.6-90 ppm of EtOH at 5-40 °C",
      p.9; storage -45 to +85 C, an absolute rating, p.15): powered with no shutdown across the envelope and both margins (bay
      air 52.55 C at +40 C, 67.55 and 70.00 C at the line); REQ-042's VOC level set from the BME688's own baseline instead of
      "the SGP41's own clean-air baseline as its datasheet defines the VOC index" (its acceptance restated); its performance
      over +40 C and after storage owed to Bosch or the bench; a second BME688 takes I2C 0x77 on board E, which the deferred
      outside pod's BME688 then cannot share.
   B  the VOC channel dropped: REQ-042 restated to water on the floor and hydrogen (S-49's part); CHO-001's line and CFL-002
      restated; U17 and its switch off board E.
   C  the SGP41 kept, its channel reported as not covered (REQ-042: "a state outside a sensing part's published range is
      reported as not covered by that channel, never assumed") while its reference reads over 49.0 C (on the east wall's skin:
      lid closed above about +34.24 to +37.77 C ambient at 32.53's 1.5 to 2.0 W/K, lid open above about +38.55 C at the line)
      and after storage outside 5 to 30 C until Sensirion states otherwise: a restriction of the VOC channel inside the
      envelope, which D-02a does not grant today.
   The session's recommendation: A, the one option that keeps a powered VOC channel across the envelope and the margins with a
   part the kit already carries. The radios' route (5) does not depend on the answer.
6c Escalation is not limited to 6b. If T-H1 reads under 2.159 W/K lid open, E5 fails for the +70 C class unless the plate
   coupling of 4e holds them (at 2.000 W/K E3-O's mixed air is 68.543 C, under +70 C, while E5's under the hold is 70.793 C,
   over it); under 1.806 W/K E3-O fails as well. Each case is assessed against the routes then left (the plate coupling's
   evidence, wider-rated parts) before any question; what would then go to the owner is a device-set re-pick (CHO-001) or a
   stated deviation of E3-O's configuration.

