   (l4e9_power_path.out at aa897e38, not pinned here: that output quotes this record). The 8.40 W with no document are Xenarc
   709GNK 6.03 W, WiFi link card 2 (standby) 1.30 W, VHF PA 30 W 1.07 W, no fan among them. Their heat is inside the case and
   inside every heat figure of 8a. Per mode (MODELED, battery side, plan; low..high at the load pins):
      PS-IDLE-SPEC (the profile)   4 fans: 3.128 W at the pack of 42.824 W (7.3 %), 75.1 Wh a day; at the loads 1.86 .. 2.97 .. 4.68 W
      PS-TYP                       4 fans: 3.112 W at the pack of 62.958 W (4.9 %), 74.7 Wh a day; at the loads 1.86 .. 2.97 .. 4.68 W
      PS-RED, lid closed           2 fans: 2.000 W at the pack of 22.205 W (9.0 %), 48.0 Wh a day; at the loads 1.14 .. 1.95 .. 3.56 W
      the heat stage (PS-SURV-R)   2 fans: 2.000 W at the pack of 23.272 W (8.6 %), 48.0 Wh a day; at the loads 1.14 .. 1.95 .. 3.56 W
      E5's hold                    2 fans: 2.010 W at the pack of 18.152 W (11.1 %), 48.2 Wh a day; at the loads 1.14 .. 1.95 .. 3.56 W
   The picked fans' power moves both budgets: at the representatives' low and high figures E5's hold carries 18.616 to 21.236 W
   into the case and its line is 2.071 to 2.333 W/K (0.100 W/K per W); the profile at the fans' high figures is 44.557 W against
   42.824 W, so a runtime falls to 0.961 of its value (MODELED). Register row drafted for L4-E9's downstream register (its owner
   inserts it): "R-new | EVIDENCE | The five fans' power (D-18, REQ-043): the picked fans' maker's figures at the duty the
   controls set replace pwr_budget.py's representative rows; E5's line moves 0.100 W/K per W into the case and the profile by
   the fans' battery-side watts | L4-E12 8c | Layer 6 components with D-18 | a held sheet; T-H1 logs the fans' drawn power".
8d T-H1: WHO AND HOW. TEST-PLAN section 8's row: "a current-moulding Peli 1450 with the 1450PF frame and a 3 mm aluminium plate
   blank; 20, 40 and 60 W of resistive heat on a dummy stack, the fans running and stopped, lid open and closed, thermocouples
   on the air, the plate, the walls and a dummy pack block"; "it needs no built kit, and its purchase is the owner's to
   authorise". Hardware (READY-TO-ACT.md 5.2): the Peli 1450 with the 1450PF frame and a 3 mm plate blank, stack heaters of 6.8
   ohm at 12.0 V giving 21.2 W each, Pico Technology PicoLog TC-08, SKU PP222, 8 thermocouple inputs, "Same Sky CFM-6025BG68, 12
   V, the -22 variant (tachometer and PWM)". No electronics are needed. Who: the prototype bench, as Layer 9's physical
   verification, once the owner authorises it (READY-TO-ACT lists what is missing: "who runs the test and where (the session
   cannot)"); a laboratory only for a chamber run at E5's +60 C (the owner's spend). The draft procedure is
   T-H1-PROCEDURE-DRAFT.md beside this record.
   Method: the dummy heaters spread as the model spreads E5's hold (W, plan): board B (slot 3, its switch, hubs, supervisors,
   the device rail) 12.06; fans (the real fans, run from the bench supply) 1.95; board A 1.81; board C and the face 1.50; the
   front end and the charger (boards E and A, on shore) 1.35; board E 0.83, plus the ballasts' 2.09 W on board A; one heater's
   21.2 W puts the line's 9.8 K rise on the air (two: 19.6 K). Points: two powers (21.2 and 42.4 W), lid open and closed, fans
   on and off: 8 points. Steady state: the time constant C/G is 0.78 to 2.27 h (32.53's 8 to 10 kJ/K, the kit's mass, an upper
   bound for an empty case, over W4's lid-open 1.22 to 2.85 W/K); within 1 % of the rise after 3.6 to 10.5 h a point, 29 to 84 h
   in all; a point ends when the mixed air drifts at most 0.1 K/h over an hour (ASSUMPTION).
   Uncertainty (ASSUMPTION, standard, k = 1): each thermocouple +-0.2 K after an isothermal comparison, the mixed air's spread
   +-0.3 K, the ambient's drift +-0.3 K, the steady-state residual 0.129 K (the drift times the line's 1.29 h), so the rise
   +-0.526 K; the power +-0.7 %, the leads +-0.5 %. Expanded (k = 2): 10.7 % at a 10 K rise and 5.5 % at 20 K. PASS LINE: the
   measured conductance, lid open with the fans, less its expanded uncertainty, at or over 2.159 W/K, so a reading of at least
   2.416 W/K at a 10 K rise (2.285 W/K at 20 K). A room reading under-reads the margin: the outside films' radiation is 5.21
   W/m2K at the room's 22 C and 7.45 W/m2K at E5's 60 C, so on W4's films the margin's conductance is 1.15 to 1.20 times the
   room's (INFERRED, a credit the pass line does not take).
8e A FAILED READING AND THE FALLBACKS. Mixed air at a lid-open, fans-on reading G (MODELED; E3-O the heat stage, E5 the hold):
      G 2.100 W/K: E3-O 67.90 C (holds), E5 70.28 C (past +70 C)
      G 2.000 W/K: E3-O 68.54 C (holds), E5 70.79 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.900 W/K: E3-O 69.26 C (holds), E5 71.36 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.806 W/K: E3-O 70.00 C (holds), E5 71.95 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.666 W/K: E3-O 71.25 C (past +70 C), E5 72.95 C (past +70 C)
      G 1.500 W/K: E3-O 73.06 C (past +70 C), E5 74.39 C (past +70 C)
   A reading in (1.806, 2.159) W/K: E3-O holds as stated, E5 under the hold passes +70 C for the class of 8a. A reading under
   1.806 W/K: E3-O passes it too. The fallbacks inside the rulings (no vent, the Peli 1450 kept), each with what it buys:
   F1 FINS ON THE PLATE (no penetration; bonded or machined; INFERRED from W4's films, k the effective area multiplier): G for
      (inside k, outside k) = (1, 1) 1.222, (1, 1.5) 1.314, (1, 2) 1.376, (1, 3) 1.453, (2, 2) 1.667, (3, 3) 2.111 in the low
      case and (1, 1) 2.850, (1, 1.5) 3.062, (1, 2) 3.224, (1, 3) 3.453, (2, 2) 3.568, (3, 3) 4.286 in the high case; outside
      fins alone saturate at the inside film (1.690 and 4.411 W/K with an endless outside area). Applied to a reading through
      W4's split, outside fins of twice the area multiply it by 1.125 to 1.131 and fins of twice the area on both faces by 1.252
      to 1.363: a reading of 1.806 W/K would read 2.261 to 2.462 W/K (both faces). T-H1's plate and wall readings give the split
      the reading actually has. Feasibility: CONDITIONAL on the face's free area (the monitor, the e-paper, the switches) and
      the lid's clearance (CASE-MARGINS M3); the session's (Layer 7).
   F2 CONDUCTION FROM THE HOT BOARDS TO THE PLATE: heat Q_c led into the plate leaves the air's balance by Q_c (1 - f), f the
      plate's fraction, so E5 at +70 C needs Q_c = (Q - 10 G) / (1 - f): G 2.000: 5.76 / 2.97; G 1.900: 9.39 / 4.84; G 1.806:
      12.82 / 6.60 (W at f 0.725 / 0.465). Board B carries 12.06 W of the hold's heat (the module, its switch, the supervisors,
      the hubs). Feasibility: CONDITIONAL on a pad path from those parts to the plate (Layer 7); the session's.
   F3 SHEDDING IN E5 (E5 requires logging only): the heat a reading allows, 10 G - 2.09 W: G 2.100: 18.91 W; G 2.000: 17.91 W; G
      1.900: 16.91 W; G 1.806: 15.97 W; G 1.666: 14.57 W; G 1.500: 12.91 W. A deeper hold that keeps the logging (the module
      idle on its own storage, board E's controller and sensors, the fans, the panel for the SOS, the supervisors and hubs on
      the logging path) and turns off KSZ9897R AVDDL+DVDDL 1.2 V 1.452 W, KSZ9897R AVDDH 2.5 V 0.825 W, KSZ9897R VDDIO 3.3 V
      0.264 W, NVMe slot 3 0.900 W, PCIe switch 3.3 V slot 3 0.355 W, PCIe switch 1.0 V slot 3 0.270 W, LG290P GNSS 0.327 W
      takes E5's heat to 13.429 W and its line to 1.552 W/K. The session's (E5's stated configuration); CONDITIONAL on a supply
      switch for each (none read for the switch chip: a Layer 8 item) and on the logging path.
   F4 THE PLATE COUPLING (4e): the RockBLOCK, board D (SA868, PCM2912A, G6K) and the LimeSDR on pads to the plate sit at the
      plate, at most the ambient plus 0.725 of the rise: E5 holds them to 1.564 W/K and E3-O to 1.309 W/K. The parts left in the
      mixed air then set the floor: the +80 C connectors (2199119-3, 2199230-4, MDT420M02001, TYPE-C-31-M-12) in the exhaust
      need 1.253 W/K in E5 and 1.399 W/K in E3-O (1.083 out of the exhaust); the H5007NL, the ATP16 and the PXP4043/C take
      section 6's wider parts or statements. So F4 holds E5 down to 1.564 W/K and E3-O down to 1.399 W/K (1.309 with the
      connectors out of the exhaust); with F3, E5 down to 1.125 W/K. With the fans stopped the coupled parts stay at most 69.82
      C (8b). Feasibility: the pads' own rise and their mechanical path (Layer 7); the session's.
   THE BEST FALLBACK: F4, the plate coupling, with F3 in E5: no owner ruling, no change to E3-O. What needs the owner: a reading
   under E3-O's F4 floor (1.399 W/K, or 1.309 W/K with the connectors out of the exhaust) leaves a deviation of E3-O's
   configuration (the hold in E3-O) or a device-set re-pick (CHO-001); the SGP41 is 6b's question already.

9 Predicates
   P1 pwr_budget and pwr_red2 reproduced byte for byte before any figure: PASS
   P2 T-H1's floor and the inside air reproduce L4-E10's 1.6664 W/K, 70.00 and 75.00 C: PASS
   P3 the acceptance is read: survive and recover, the CM5 not shut down, the monitor and radios on, C1's shedding recorded, E5 logging: PASS
   P4 every fitted line, module and undeclared line is screened: PASS
   P5 every line the first pass finds within reach is read one by one, rated to +80 C or more and over only in the exhaust, or the regulators of 5c: PASS
   P6 approach (a)'s line is over the low-case outer-film cap and under W4's high case: PASS
   P7 the route keeps E3-O as stated: every radio on (work) at E3-O, no hold there: PASS
   P8 at the line every part routed by the air is inside its governing limit at the mixed air at both margins: PASS
   P9 the hold lowers the enclosure line: G_c under G_a: PASS
   P10 the owner question is raised only after the routes are assessed: for the SGP41 in the envelope, and for no part at the margins: PASS
   P11 every judged limit names its category and none is cleared on an absolute rating alone (the SGP41 on Table 4): PASS
   P12 the SGP41 is off before its local +55 C and its output is used only at or under Table 4's +50 C (printed error, gradient, lag, rounded down): PASS
   P13 the hold's window exists at the line only with a calibrated reference (e_allow over 0) and not across the whole exhaust spread: PASS
   P14 no location holds the SGP41 to Table 4 in the envelope: the coolest skin's line over every lid-closed conductance held, storage outside Table 4: PASS
   P15 the lines' basis: Q over the room to +70 C gives 2.159, 1.806 and 2.709 W/K, and E5's heat is its loads, losses and shore loss summed: PASS
   P16 the fans' power is counted: rv-pwr's rows, load_trace's tier-R rows in the 42.8 W profile the replay carries, none among its W with no document: PASS
   P17 T-H1's pass line lies over 2.159 W/K by its expanded uncertainty and every point reaches steady state in a stated time: PASS
   P18 the plate coupling holds E5 and E3-O below E3-O's line, and the deeper hold lowers E5's heat (the session's fallbacks): PASS

